# ZERO-TOKEN CONTEXT & ARCHITECTURAL RULES
# Project: Enterprise Authentication SaaS (EA SaaS)

[IDENTITY & VOCABULARY]
- Official Full Title: Enterprise Authentication SaaS
- Permitted Short Title: EA SaaS
- Never use alternative product names or generic placeholders.

[ZERO-TOKEN DIRECTORY BOUNDARIES]
1. UI Components:
   - Reusable primitives live strictly in `src/components/ui/`
   - Feature-specific UI lives strictly in `src/features/<module>/components/`
   - Never write raw business logic or DB calls inside `.tsx` files.

2. Server Services & Actions:
   - Server Actions and services live in `src/features/<module>/server/`
   - All server operations must accept and return Zod-validated schemas defined in `src/features/<module>/types/`

3. Multi-Tenant Scoping:
   - Every database query must explicitly filter by `organization_id` or `tenant_id`.
   - Never query user records across tenant boundaries without permission validation.

4. Audit Logging Rule:
   - Every state-mutating operation (login, role update, 2FA toggle, session revoke) MUST call `logAuditEvent()`.

5. Documentation Sync:
   - When introducing new routes or server actions, immediately update `docs/06_CODING_HANDOVER.md`.
